From 2660b299e1567dee53c308cb2528da268b278d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 392/488] soh: name the 27 address-named symbols defined in
 z_kaleido_scope_PAL.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 27 are defined in soh/src/overlays/misc/ovl_kaleido_scope/z_kaleido_scope_PAL.c.

  * D_8082AD40 -> sCursorColorPhase
    deduced, confidence HIGH: which of the four cursor colour phases is
    active

  * D_8082AD44 -> sStickXRepeatTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the repeat delay for horizontal stick input on
    the pause pages

  * D_8082AD48 -> sStickYRepeatTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the repeat delay for vertical stick input

  * D_8082AD4C -> sStickXDir
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the horizontal direction that repeat is
    currently firing in

  * D_8082AD50 -> sStickYDir
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the vertical direction that repeat is
    currently firing in

  * D_8082AD78 -> sInfoPanelLeftTextures
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the per-page, per-language texture for the
    left half of the info panel

  * D_8082ADA8 -> sInfoPanelRightTextures
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the same table for the right half, rotated by
    one page

  * D_8082ADD8 -> sInfoPanelLeftWidths
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the width of the left info panel text in each
    language

  * D_8082ADE0 -> sInfoPanelRightWidths
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the width of the right info panel text in each
    language

  * D_8082ADE8 -> sInfoPanelPromptWidths
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the width of the third info panel string in
    each language

  * D_8082ADF0 -> sInfoPanelColorSets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the two RGBA sets the info panel text
    alternates between

  * D_8082AE00 -> sInfoPanelFadeTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts that alternation down and reloads from
    ZREG(28)

  * D_8082AE04 -> sInfoPanelColorIdx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: which of those two sets the panel is easing
    toward

  * D_8082AE08 -> sUnusedAreaIndices
    deduced, confidence GUESS: a twenty-entry area index table nothing in
    the overlay reads; sAreaGsIndices covers the twelve the world map
    actually uses

  * D_8082AE30 -> sAreaGsIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: maps a world map cursor position onto the gold
    skulltula area index

  * D_808321A0 -> sInfoPanelR
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the current red of the info panel text

  * D_808321A2 -> sInfoPanelG
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the current green of the info panel text

  * D_808321A4 -> sInfoPanelB
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the current blue of the info panel text

  * D_808321A6 -> sInfoPanelA
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the current alpha of the info panel text

  * D_8082B110 -> sPromptBounceOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the vertical offset the page prompt quad
    bounces by

  * D_8082B114 -> sPromptBounceTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts that bounce down

  * D_8082B118 -> sPromptBouncePhase
    deduced, confidence HIGH: which half of the bounce cycle is running

  * D_8082B258 -> sNextPauseState
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the pause state installed once the transition
    timer expires

  * D_8082B25C -> sPauseStateTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts that transition, and the save prompt,
    down

  * D_8082B260 -> sCursorFadeSteps
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the number of steps the game-over cursor
    colour fade is divided into

  * D_8082ACF4 -> sPageCursorColorSets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the twelve cursor colour sets
    KaleidoScope_DrawPages eases toward, four overridable from the cosmetics
    editor; named PageCursor because z_kaleido_collect.c owns the plain
    sCursorColorSets

  * D_8082AD3C -> sPageCursorFadeTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: counts that fade down and reloads from the
    ZREG step lengths; named to match sPageCursorColorSets

